  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-07-30T18:26:46.925Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There are three points to this entry:\n- The calibration mirror should NOT follow the head rotation. It is disorienting to say the least, and makes calibrating more difficult.\n- The calibration mirror should not appear if main mirror is active.\n- The calibration mirror should stay on for 3~5 seconds. After finishing the calibration, one must make sure the avatar calibrated properly, and repeat the process if needed. It will be best if the mirror persists throughout the entire process, disappearing either on a timer or on a trigger click (preferably both).",
